## Research Validity (Section 40 of the outline / positioning statement)

This environment sits alongside procedurally-regenerable, rule-explicit benchmarks (in the spirit of ARC-AGI's
train/held-out generalization split, and structured-reasoning puzzle benchmarks like Sudoku variants) but adds
continuous, physically-motivated dynamics and long-horizon planning, which those benchmarks generally lack.
Its defining property is the one called out repeatedly above: **the underlying causal rules are fixed and
learnable through interaction, while the surface layout (map, seed) is freely regenerable** — so a
train/held-out split (Section 33) can isolate genuine world-model transfer from layout memorization, the same
way ARC-AGI isolates rule abstraction from surface-pattern matching, but here applied to a continuous,
partially-stochastic physical simulation rather than static grids.

