## SECTION 41 (design mistakes) — Compliance Check

This spec was checked against all 13 listed anti-patterns: no terrain carries a flat energy multiplier (every
output traces through Sections 6–13's chained equations); "mountain=good wind" and "sand=good solar" are both
false in general within this model (a leeward mountain cell has *worse* wind, per RULE-WIND-003; sand's solar
output depends entirely on sun/cloud/obstruction, not a sand bonus); weather randomness is seeded and bounded
(Section 36); rules are fully disclosed as discoverable-through-interaction (Section 21); the physics model is
deliberately simplified to remain playable (every equation is explicitly `[GAME APPROXIMATION]` or
`[PHYSICS-BASED, simplified]`, never claimed as a full scientific simulator); levels differ by mechanic
introduction, not just map size (Section 21); money is one of ten scoring metrics, not the sole objective
(Section 28); no single technology dominates by construction (Section 37); no invented pseudo-scientific terms
lack computational meaning (every named variable appears in an equation); update order is fixed precisely to
prevent circular dependencies (Section 24); invalid states are prevented at placement time rather than
resolved at runtime (Section 35); and determinism is a hard requirement (Section 36).

