## I. Top 20 Test Cases

1. Mass balance: rainfall = infiltration+runoff+evaporation exactly, every cell, every tick.
2. Energy conservation: generation ≥ delivered+loss+curtailed, every tick.
3. Determinism: identical seed+action log → identical state hash across 2 runs.
4. Wind shadow: leeward turbine output strictly less than an identical windward turbine, same wind speed.
5. Rain shadow: leeward-of-ridge cloud formation strictly less likely than windward, same humidity input.
6. Solar at night: `sunElevation≤0` → `solarOutput=0` exactly, never negative.
7. Turbine below cutIn: `windOutput=0` exactly.
8. Turbine above cutOut: `windOutput=0` exactly (safety shutdown).
9. Hydro with `Q<Q_min`: output forced to 0, no divide-by-zero.
10. Snowmelt cannot exceed available `snowDepth` in a single tick.
11. River flow never negative; confluence `Q` equals sum of contributing `Q`s.
12. Placement on invalid terrain always returns INVALID with a specific, non-generic reason string.
13. Reinforced Mud passes the stability≥0.7 check only after the documented overlay stack is present.
14. Floating Solar rejected on a river cell above `V_float_max`.
15. Machine at end-of-life produces exactly 0 output regardless of environmental inputs.
16. Cable overload curtails exactly the excess above `capacity`, delivers exactly `capacity`.
17. Two incompatible machines can never both occupy one cell (placement-time prevention only, no runtime state).
18. Generalization gap test: agent score on held-out map vs. training map, flag if gap exceeds a threshold.
19. Memory test: agent's second-encounter response time/accuracy on a repeated event pattern improves vs. first.
20. Anti-memorization probe: an agent using only a fixed terrain→machine lookup table scores materially below
    an agent that reasons from current wind/sun/cloud/water state, on the same held-out map.

